---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About Kidtivity Lab"
  description="Why we built Kidtivity Lab: practical activities that fit real life — short attention spans, messy living rooms, and all."
>
  <EditorialPage
    eyebrow="About Kidtivity Lab"
    title="Play doesn’t need to be a project"
    lede="We help parents turn ordinary afternoons, rainy mornings, and restless ten-minute gaps into moments that feel good for everyone."
    currentLabel="About"
    wide
  >
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Made for real-life parenting</h2>
      <p>
        Kidtivity Lab exists for one very familiar moment: it’s late afternoon, your child is
        bored, and you have ten minutes plus whatever happens to be in the kitchen drawer. You
        should not need a shopping trip, an hour of preparation, or a perfect craft room to make
        that moment fun.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our activities are designed for busy adults and curious kids. They are quick to understand,
        easy to adapt, and specific enough that you can start without having to invent the missing
        steps yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
      <div class="card-grid-copy">
        <article class="copy-card">
          <span class="copy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span>
          <h3>Activity Finder</h3>
          <p>Filter by age, place, time, materials, and the kind of moment your family needs.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="copy-card">
          <span class="copy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
          <h3>Practical activity guides</h3>
          <p>Clear materials, short steps, helpful variations, and visible safety notes.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="copy-card">
          <span class="copy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</span>
          <h3>Print-and-play resources</h3>
          <p>Simple packs for travel, quiet time, seasonal days, and screen-free play.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Our principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Useful in under 30 seconds.</strong> The answer comes before the backstory.</li>
        <li><strong>Realistic materials.</strong> Household basics beat a specialist supply list.</li>
        <li><strong>No parenting guilt.</strong> This is an idea library, not another standard to meet.</li>
        <li><strong>Age-aware, not rigid.</strong> Kids develop differently, so every idea can be adapted.</li>
        <li><strong>Safety stays visible.</strong> Important notes belong next to the activity, not in fine print.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>How activities are prepared</h2>
      <p>
        Each activity is reviewed for clarity, setup time, age fit, required materials, and common
        safety considerations. We favor ideas that invite imagination or connection instead of
        producing a Pinterest-perfect final result.
      </p>
      <div class="note-box">
        Kidtivity Lab is an informational resource for parents and caregivers. You know your child
        best—adapt every activity to their abilities, interests, and current level of supervision.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Help us make it better</h2>
      <p>
        Found a confusing step? Have a household favorite we should test? We would love to hear
        from you. Visit the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:info@kidtivitylab.com">info@kidtivitylab.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </EditorialPage>
</Base>
